  <data name="whatIs" xml:space="preserve"><value>What is a nonogram?</value></data>
  <data name="whatIsBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>A nonogram is a picture hidden inside numbers. The clues on each row and column tell you how many blocks to fill and in what order. Work out every line with pure logic and a picture appears — you never have to guess.</value></data>
  <data name="alsoCalled" xml:space="preserve"><value>Also known as: Picross · Griddler · Hanjie · Pic-a-Pix · Paint by Numbers · Japanese crossword</value></data>
  <data name="aboutHowTo" xml:space="preserve"><value>How to Play</value></data>
  <data name="aboutPrivacy" xml:space="preserve"><value>Privacy policy</value></data>
  <data name="aboutRate" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rate squarebuzz</value></data>
  <data name="ht1" xml:space="preserve"><value>Read the clues</value></data>
  <data name="ht1b" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each number is one unbroken run of filled blocks, listed in order. Row clue 3 1 means three together, at least one gap, then one on its own.</value></data>
  <data name="ht2" xml:space="preserve"><value>Fill and cross</value></data>
  <data name="ht2b" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tap a square to fill it. Switch to X mode for squares you have proved stay empty. X marks are not decoration — they are how you keep track.</value></data>
  <data name="ht3" xml:space="preserve"><value>Overlap on long clues</value></data>
  <data name="ht3b" xml:space="preserve"><value>In a 10-wide row a clue of 8 must cover the middle 6 squares no matter where it starts. Push the run left, push it right, and fill whatever overlaps.</value></data>
  <data name="ht4" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cross-reference</value></data>
  <data name="ht4b" xml:space="preserve"><value>When a row gives you one certain block, look down that column. The new block often finishes a column clue, which gives you more Xs, which gives you more blocks.</value></data>
  <data name="ht5" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cross out finished lines</value></data>
  <data name="ht5b" xml:space="preserve"><value>When a line matches its clues completely, X every remaining square in it. The clue numbers fade so you know that line is done.</value></data>
